program Constants.
note The SI defining constants (exact by definition since 20 May 2019; BIPM, The International System of
note Units, 9th edition, Table 1) and constants derived from them exactly. Values are in SI units; the
note kernel keeps them as exact rationals, so a product such as R = N_A k is exact too.

term "speed of light" means "exactly 299 792 458 metres per second (the SI defining constant c)".
term "Avogadro constant" means "exactly 6.022 140 76 × 10^23 per mole (N_A)".
term "Boltzmann constant" means "exactly 1.380 649 × 10^-23 joules per kelvin (k)".
term "elementary charge" means "exactly 1.602 176 634 × 10^-19 coulombs (e)".
term "Planck constant" means "exactly 6.626 070 15 × 10^-34 joule seconds (h)".
term "standard gravity" means "exactly 9.806 65 metres per second squared (g_n)".
term "standard atmosphere" means "exactly 101 325 pascals".

note Defining constants: caesium hyperfine frequency (Hz), c (m/s), h (J s), e (C), k (J/K), N_A (1/mol), K_cd (lm/W).
note Import it qualified (import constants as si.) and write si.planck, or import the names you use.
let caesium_frequency = 9192631770.
let speed_of_light = 299792458.
let planck = 6.62607015e-34.
let elementary_charge = 1.602176634e-19.
let boltzmann = 1.380649e-23.
let avogadro = 6.02214076e23.
let luminous_efficacy = 683.
note Exact derived constants: molar gas constant R = N_A k (J/(mol K)), Faraday constant F = N_A e (C/mol),
note the reduced Planck constant needs pi (a 30-place decimal), so it is a function of the kernel's pi.
let gas_constant = avogadro * boltzmann.
let faraday = avogadro * elementary_charge.
let standard_gravity = 9.80665.
let standard_atmosphere = 101325.
function reduced_planck() -> Number = planck / (2 * pi).
note Convenience: photon energy E = h f (J) and wavelength from frequency (m).
function photon_energy(f: Number) -> Number = planck * f.
function wavelength(f: Number) -> Number = speed_of_light / f.

test "derived constants are exact" do
  assert gas_constant = 8.31446261815324.
  assert faraday = 96485.3321233100184.
  assert photon_energy(1) = planck.
end.
